WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.229 --> 00:00:02.159
Hey Thoughty2 here.

00:00:02.159 --> 00:00:08.430
Facebook boasts over 2.2 billion loyal subjects
and the average social minion regularly shares

00:00:08.430 --> 00:00:14.089
their opinions about their favourite cold
sandwich meats with their family and 300 other

00:00:14.089 --> 00:00:16.680
people they once met in a room somewhere.

00:00:16.680 --> 00:00:21.419
Their relationship status, snapshots of their
every day and the most intimate details of

00:00:21.419 --> 00:00:23.550
their life, they share also.

00:00:23.550 --> 00:00:28.939
Your Facebook timeline is a written and highly
detailed history of your life.

00:00:28.939 --> 00:00:34.160
And as we all know, a wise man once said “If
you can describe your life on one sheet of

00:00:34.160 --> 00:00:37.190
paper, then you need to turn a new page.”

00:00:37.190 --> 00:00:41.770
No one actually ever said that, but I couldn’t
find a meanful quote to put here, so that

00:00:41.770 --> 00:00:42.780
will have to do.

00:00:42.780 --> 00:00:48.870
But just how much do Facebook and other internet
giants like Microsoft, Google, Amazon and

00:00:48.870 --> 00:00:51.379
Apple know about you?

00:00:51.379 --> 00:00:56.760
How many secret data points have they cherry-picked
from your tree of life and what do they do

00:00:56.760 --> 00:00:59.750
with all those sweet, succulent data cherries?

00:00:59.750 --> 00:01:05.590
I’ll tell you what they do, they bake them
into a delicious money pie, with a big fat

00:01:05.590 --> 00:01:07.260
advert on top of it.

00:01:07.260 --> 00:01:13.940
And your privacy is the metaphorical pastry,
so what can you do to stop it from crumbling

00:01:13.940 --> 00:01:14.940
to pieces?

00:01:14.940 --> 00:01:19.200
Let me ask you, have you ever been searching
for something on the web such as toasters,

00:01:19.200 --> 00:01:23.890
pet food or restaurants in your area that
aren’t completely terrible and then you

00:01:23.890 --> 00:01:25.670
open up Facebook and boom!

00:01:25.670 --> 00:01:31.140
You see adverts for toasters, pet food and
not-crap local restaurants, or whatever other

00:01:31.140 --> 00:01:34.100
internet goodies you may have been ogling.

00:01:34.100 --> 00:01:39.030
It probably happens to you all the time and
you either ignore it, chalk it up as yet another

00:01:39.030 --> 00:01:43.930
massive coincidence or you start to get all
weird and suspicious, and make a tinfoil hat

00:01:43.930 --> 00:01:44.980
for your hamster.

00:01:44.980 --> 00:01:51.090
And suspicious you should be because the truth
is that for a long time now, Facebook has

00:01:51.090 --> 00:01:57.930
been stalking you around the entire web like
some kind of benevolent wealthy pedophile.

00:01:57.930 --> 00:02:03.740
Yes Facebook attorneys, I’m aware your services
have a minimum age limit, please don’t sue

00:02:03.740 --> 00:02:04.740
me.

00:02:04.740 --> 00:02:09.229
Facebook has always been completely free for
its users and that’s because it’s users,

00:02:09.229 --> 00:02:11.659
you, are what’s being sold.

00:02:11.659 --> 00:02:17.490
There’s a well-known saying that I just
made up, “If a service is free, then you

00:02:17.490 --> 00:02:19.380
are the product”.

00:02:19.380 --> 00:02:23.230
You are what Facebook sells, all your lovely
data.

00:02:23.230 --> 00:02:27.629
Facebook sells to advertisers the ability
to target their adverts and their products

00:02:27.629 --> 00:02:33.340
to Facebook users in really specific and creepy
ways based on the data that Facebook has on

00:02:33.340 --> 00:02:34.340
you.

00:02:34.340 --> 00:02:38.769
Say a company comes along that makes and sells
ice cream, for a price Facebook will allow

00:02:38.769 --> 00:02:43.820
that advertiser to advertise their delicious
ice cream to every Facebook user who is a

00:02:43.820 --> 00:02:49.980
hetrosexual female between the ages of 30
and 50 who recently ended a long term relationship

00:02:49.980 --> 00:02:55.640
and has also had a string of previous long
term relationships, and also happens to own

00:02:55.640 --> 00:02:59.000
two cats and isn’t lactose intolerant.

00:02:59.000 --> 00:03:02.379
And who also lives in Nantucket, whilst they’re
at it, just because they can.

00:03:02.379 --> 00:03:07.829
Now, I don’t mean to stereotype, but this
kind of specificity is exactly what advertisers

00:03:07.829 --> 00:03:14.760
are looking for and Facebook has the ability
to offer that juicy data, unlike almost any

00:03:14.760 --> 00:03:17.349
other company on Earth.

00:03:17.349 --> 00:03:22.040
Because Facebook knows secrets about you,
things that would make your grandma slap you

00:03:22.040 --> 00:03:25.450
in your ruddy little face if she ever found
out.

00:03:25.450 --> 00:03:30.779
There have been rumours spreading around the
internet recently that Facebook uses people’s

00:03:30.779 --> 00:03:37.879
microphones on their smartphones and devices
to covertly record their conversations 24/7.

00:03:37.879 --> 00:03:43.819
Then algorithms analyse that speech to identify
what that person may be interested in and

00:03:43.819 --> 00:03:46.489
thus show them advertisements for it.

00:03:46.489 --> 00:03:51.250
I know what you’re thinking, “whoah slow
down there Thoughty2, you’ll be making tinfoil

00:03:51.250 --> 00:03:54.550
hats, scarves and gloves before the end of
this video”.

00:03:54.550 --> 00:04:01.090
But there have been thousands of reports across
the web and even videos of people talking

00:04:01.090 --> 00:04:05.420
about something out loud in front of their
phone, for example discussing their holiday

00:04:05.420 --> 00:04:12.670
plans to France and then logging into Facebook
later and seeing ads for villas in France.

00:04:12.670 --> 00:04:14.370
So what’s the deal here?

00:04:14.370 --> 00:04:15.890
Is there any truth to this?

00:04:15.890 --> 00:04:20.140
Is Facebook a naughty nancy, spying on us
through our phones’ microphones?

00:04:20.140 --> 00:04:27.780
The reassuringly disappointing reality is
that the expense, resources and enormous processing

00:04:27.780 --> 00:04:35.340
power required to record, perform vocal recognition
and run an algorithm on billions of audio

00:04:35.340 --> 00:04:43.680
feeds 24 hours a day is, with current technology,
completely impossible, even with the resources

00:04:43.680 --> 00:04:46.640
of all the big tech companies combined.

00:04:46.640 --> 00:04:51.730
So the likelihood that Facebook or any other
tech giant is using your microphone to spy

00:04:51.730 --> 00:04:59.130
on you is really, really small and ex-Facebook
employees have said that it’s just not technically

00:04:59.130 --> 00:05:02.700
or legally possible for Facebook to do that.

00:05:02.700 --> 00:05:09.690
But the scary truth and why I’m fairly confident
that Facebook aren’t recording us is that

00:05:09.690 --> 00:05:11.260
they don’t need to.

00:05:11.260 --> 00:05:17.010
Seriously, they wouldn’t actually gain much
and the potential risks are enormous.

00:05:17.010 --> 00:05:19.210
And why wouldn’t they gain anything?

00:05:19.210 --> 00:05:23.820
Because they can already find out everything
they need to know about you without listening

00:05:23.820 --> 00:05:25.930
to a single conversation.

00:05:25.930 --> 00:05:32.260
Facebook’s algorithms are so sophisticated
and their data harvesting net is so unfathomably

00:05:32.260 --> 00:05:38.850
wide that they can already build a complete
history of your life, a comprehensive profile

00:05:38.850 --> 00:05:44.020
of your likes, dislikes, where you’ve been,
where you’re likely to go and what you’re

00:05:44.020 --> 00:05:50.500
likely to purchase just solely based on your
online activity.

00:05:50.500 --> 00:05:55.190
And now you’re sat there wishing you hadn’t
shopped online for avocado slicers for 4 hours

00:05:55.190 --> 00:05:56.430
on Sunday.

00:05:56.430 --> 00:06:02.640
But what you might not know about Facebook’s
data harvesting net is just how wide those

00:06:02.640 --> 00:06:06.400
greedy data fishermen spread it.

00:06:06.400 --> 00:06:11.930
Everything you do on Facebook itself, whether
through the website or app is collected and

00:06:11.930 --> 00:06:18.760
stored - private messages, status updates,
likes, dislikes, comments and location data.

00:06:18.760 --> 00:06:22.440
But it doesn’t stop at the Facebook app.

00:06:22.440 --> 00:06:27.170
What if I told you that Facebook and many
other advertising companies, follow you around

00:06:27.170 --> 00:06:35.590
the entire internet, tracking your every website
visit, and interaction.

00:06:35.590 --> 00:06:41.640
You know those like and share buttons you
see on 99% of websites, that no one uses ever.

00:06:41.640 --> 00:06:45.840
And all those sites that use “Login with
Facebook”?

00:06:45.840 --> 00:06:50.460
For a web developer to put these features
into a web page they have to make a pact with

00:06:50.460 --> 00:06:53.310
Facebook, written in code and blood.

00:06:53.310 --> 00:06:59.140
That they will include a line of Javascript
tracking code on their website, some refer

00:06:59.140 --> 00:07:03.800
to it as the Facebook pixel to make it sound
all cute and innocent.

00:07:03.800 --> 00:07:08.880
Every time a visitor loads a web page that
contains the Facebook pixel, and to be clear

00:07:08.880 --> 00:07:14.790
that is close to every web page you visit
on a daily basis, the pixel lets Facebook

00:07:14.790 --> 00:07:17.740
know that you’ve visited that web page.

00:07:17.740 --> 00:07:22.750
It sends back a packet of data about yourself
and your location.

00:07:22.750 --> 00:07:27.210
When you log into Facebook it places a file
called a cookie on your computer or mobile

00:07:27.210 --> 00:07:28.500
device.

00:07:28.500 --> 00:07:33.260
Most cookies go all bad and rotten and eventually
remove themselves from your computer after,

00:07:33.260 --> 00:07:38.710
30 days or so but these cookies are baked
with whatever Plutonium-based preservative

00:07:38.710 --> 00:07:45.990
McDonalds puts into their not-burgers, they
never expire and unless you find this not-so-delicious

00:07:45.990 --> 00:07:51.880
radioactive cookie yourself and delete it,
it will sit on your device forever.

00:07:51.880 --> 00:07:57.920
Now, everytime you visit a website that isn’t
Facebook, the cookie alerts the Facebook code

00:07:57.920 --> 00:08:02.770
that is most likely in that website, in the
form of a like or share button, or Login With

00:08:02.770 --> 00:08:04.280
Facebook integration.

00:08:04.280 --> 00:08:08.120
The cookie contains a unique code which identifies
your Facebook account.

00:08:08.120 --> 00:08:14.000
So the website then reports back to Facebook,
behind the scenes, it sends your IP address,

00:08:14.000 --> 00:08:18.650
your location, the browser and device you’re
using, plus other information.

00:08:18.650 --> 00:08:25.810
Like a delicious data bento box sent straight
to facebook, that contains bit of you.

00:08:25.810 --> 00:08:30.610
Facebook uses all this data to build a detailed
profile about you, including all the websites

00:08:30.610 --> 00:08:36.659
you visit, and yes, even the ones you don’t
want them to know about, you sick-o.

00:08:36.659 --> 00:08:42.079
Using all this data Facebook can accurately
work out what you’re interested in and most

00:08:42.079 --> 00:08:45.920
importantly, what you’re likely to spend
your money on.

00:08:45.920 --> 00:08:52.860
This data isn’t sold, but is leased to advertisers
who wish to target their products to a very

00:08:52.860 --> 00:08:55.050
specific audience.

00:08:55.050 --> 00:08:59.990
Facebook’s net is wide too, they don’t
just use these data collection techniques

00:08:59.990 --> 00:09:05.529
through the Facebook platform and developer
network, the data is also collected through

00:09:05.529 --> 00:09:10.839
their web of other companies, such as Instagram,
Whatsapp and of course Facebook Messenger,

00:09:10.839 --> 00:09:14.270
the three cornerstones of a moronic social
diet.

00:09:14.270 --> 00:09:20.420
All this data is funnelled into the same algorithm
to build the most complete possible profile

00:09:20.420 --> 00:09:21.710
on you.

00:09:21.710 --> 00:09:29.290
Because today, now more than ever before,
knowledge is power and data is money.

00:09:29.290 --> 00:09:35.190
So invasive is Facebook’s tracking that
they seriously annoyed the country of Belgium

00:09:35.190 --> 00:09:39.620
and if there’s one thing you don’t want
to do, it’s makes enemies with the country

00:09:39.620 --> 00:09:44.870
that gave the world chips, waffles and more
beers than you can shake a nun at.

00:09:44.870 --> 00:09:52.930
In 2016 a Belgian court attempted to sue Facebook
for shadow tracking its users across the web.

00:09:52.930 --> 00:09:58.499
The Belgian court strongly disagreed with
how Facebook secretly follows their citizens

00:09:58.499 --> 00:10:04.620
down every dark alleyway of the internet,
wearing a long blue trench coat, wielding

00:10:04.620 --> 00:10:10.920
those cold, reptilian Zuckerberg eyes that
say “we will take your data, you will enjoy

00:10:10.920 --> 00:10:11.920
it”.

00:10:11.920 --> 00:10:17.240
And they argued that Facebook doesn’t do
enough to make its users aware when and on

00:10:17.240 --> 00:10:23.740
what sites they are being tracked and their
data is being harvested in a drag-net style

00:10:23.740 --> 00:10:28.040
and us citizens are just defenseless little
tuna fish, flapping from one useless webpage

00:10:28.040 --> 00:10:29.040
to the next.

00:10:29.040 --> 00:10:35.519
It was also discovered that Facebook was also
tracking users that have never even visited

00:10:35.519 --> 00:10:37.800
the Facebook website and don’t have an account.

00:10:37.800 --> 00:10:43.480
Using their social sharing plugins that are
on every website worth more than a pound.

00:10:43.480 --> 00:10:48.769
Facebook allegendly logs the IP address, the
pages they visit and other information of

00:10:48.769 --> 00:10:53.370
website visitors, regardless if they have
a Facebook account.

00:10:53.370 --> 00:10:58.139
Even though these users have never agreed
to a Facebook privacy policy or their Terms

00:10:58.139 --> 00:11:01.809
and Conditions, which we’ve all read, haven’t
we.

00:11:01.809 --> 00:11:06.839
Thus this data is being collected illegally,
according to the Belgian court.

00:11:06.839 --> 00:11:15.110
Stoked up on delicious premium beers the Belgian
court went full on beast mode against Facebook,

00:11:15.110 --> 00:11:20.410
saying that until Facebook changes its behaviour
and stops tracking its users around the web,

00:11:20.410 --> 00:11:24.899
that it would have to pay a fine of 250,000
Euro a day.

00:11:24.899 --> 00:11:30.620
But because Facebook is wealthier than Pablo
Escobar’s left thumb, according to estimated

00:11:30.620 --> 00:11:37.439
revenue figures it takes Facebook 21 minutes
to make 250,000 Euro.

00:11:37.439 --> 00:11:42.920
Yet it was still enough of a threat to make
Zuckerberg’s empty face have an actual expression

00:11:42.920 --> 00:11:50.279
and he set his best lawyers on the Belgians
like some kind of high-stakes Pokemon battle.

00:11:50.279 --> 00:11:56.529
Initially Facebook-achu won the battle on
a technical clause, but Fast forward a couple

00:11:56.529 --> 00:12:02.959
of years, until, well now and the Belgians
hit back with a new lawsuit due to recent

00:12:02.959 --> 00:12:08.749
changes in EU law that means any EU country
can sue any company that operates or sells

00:12:08.749 --> 00:12:12.759
services within any other European country.

00:12:12.759 --> 00:12:18.569
This time those Belgian beauties won, the
court deemed that by anonymously following

00:12:18.569 --> 00:12:23.519
people around the internet and collecting
data on them that Facebook had contravened

00:12:23.519 --> 00:12:25.769
EU privacy laws.

00:12:25.769 --> 00:12:31.529
Facebook was ordered to destroy all the unlawfully
collected data which is about as easy as clearing

00:12:31.529 --> 00:12:37.149
your disgusting internet history in Internet
bloody Explorer and they were ordered stop

00:12:37.149 --> 00:12:42.800
the practice immediately or pay $100 million
in fines.

00:12:42.800 --> 00:12:47.809
But it’s not just Facebook that knows your
prefered colour of swimwear.

00:12:47.809 --> 00:12:53.420
For many years now Apple has been building
undercover location and ad tracking technology

00:12:53.420 --> 00:12:55.529
right into their operating systems.

00:12:55.529 --> 00:13:00.649
Apple uses what they call an IDFA, a unique
identifier that your iPhone sends back to

00:13:00.649 --> 00:13:05.810
Apple every time you visit a website, download
an app or open an app.

00:13:05.810 --> 00:13:11.680
Apple shares the IDFA data with app developers
and advertisers, so that they can better target

00:13:11.680 --> 00:13:12.980
their ads toward you.

00:13:12.980 --> 00:13:19.269
Oh, and all Apple devices also track your
GPS location data and build a detailed private

00:13:19.269 --> 00:13:26.350
map of exactly where you’ve been, down to
specific addresses and businesses, concretely

00:13:26.350 --> 00:13:28.640
winning stalker of the year award.

00:13:28.640 --> 00:13:34.920
Google also does this, on both iOS and Android
devices you can actually see a map of exactly

00:13:34.920 --> 00:13:39.339
where you went and the path you took on any
given date.

00:13:39.339 --> 00:13:44.680
If you haven’t already, take a look afterwards,
it will be the creepiest thing you’ve seen

00:13:44.680 --> 00:13:46.639
in 36 minutes.

00:13:46.639 --> 00:13:52.300
All this covert data collecting makes one
think, should we be okay with allowing our

00:13:52.300 --> 00:14:00.189
personal information to be harvested like
meat and sold to the highest bidder?

00:14:00.189 --> 00:14:06.170
We all enjoy the many benefits of social networks,
apps, free email and countless other services

00:14:06.170 --> 00:14:08.959
where we, the consumer, are the product.

00:14:08.959 --> 00:14:14.420
But when all these tech companies are collecting
a permanent and detailed databank of your

00:14:14.420 --> 00:14:20.110
life, a digital version of your personality,
should we be okay with that?

00:14:20.110 --> 00:14:24.069
That’s really something for you to decide.

00:14:24.069 --> 00:14:28.759
But when our data is the product that generates
revenue, if we didn’t allow companies to

00:14:28.759 --> 00:14:32.589
harvest it then there would be no service.

00:14:32.589 --> 00:14:36.980
Your great aunt Mavis will never see that
sultry selfie you posted from the toilets

00:14:36.980 --> 00:14:42.420
of some cheap bar last Friday night, and how
utterly tragic would that be.

00:14:42.420 --> 00:14:48.709
It’s our personal data that allows companies
like Facebook and Google to exist in today’s

00:14:48.709 --> 00:14:51.740
world, where data is king.

00:14:51.740 --> 00:14:56.740
But it only seems fair that we should know
when and how our data is being collected.

00:14:56.740 --> 00:15:02.129
You’re all very aware by now of the recent
Cambridge Analytica scandal.

00:15:02.129 --> 00:15:07.540
Our data was harvested from Facebook by data
scientists in huge quantities, without our

00:15:07.540 --> 00:15:12.709
knowledge or direct consent and then that
data was analysed to target political attack

00:15:12.709 --> 00:15:16.629
ads at us online and on television.

00:15:16.629 --> 00:15:21.279
The whole thing has blown up into a scandal
so big it would make Nixon jealous.

00:15:21.279 --> 00:15:26.230
And Facebook CEO Mark Zuckerberg was made
to testify in court over the whole thing,

00:15:26.230 --> 00:15:29.200
and even worse, smile.

00:15:29.200 --> 00:15:35.439
But what makes Cambridge Analytica so utterly
scandalous is that for every user who took

00:15:35.439 --> 00:15:41.259
the quiz that harvested that user’s data,
it also spread into their network of friends

00:15:41.259 --> 00:15:45.110
and harvested their data too, without their
consent.

00:15:45.110 --> 00:15:52.459
Resulting in personal data being stolen from
87 million Facebook profiles in total.

00:15:52.459 --> 00:15:59.270
Facebook has been on defensive ever since,
but to rub salt into their wounds they are

00:15:59.270 --> 00:16:04.860
now under pressure from a new European Union
law that aims to change the way data is collected

00:16:04.860 --> 00:16:05.920
for good.

00:16:05.920 --> 00:16:10.259
It’s no coincidence that this video was
released today, the 25th May 2018, because

00:16:10.259 --> 00:16:15.750
today a new law, several years in the making
comes into effect today across the whole of

00:16:15.750 --> 00:16:16.750
Europe.

00:16:16.750 --> 00:16:22.420
It’s called GDPR or General Data Protection
Regulation and it’s the biggest slap in

00:16:22.420 --> 00:16:27.899
the face to companies that wish to anonymously
harvest our data since sliced litigation.

00:16:27.899 --> 00:16:33.509
GDPR basically means companies like Facebook
and hundreds of thousands of others that wish

00:16:33.509 --> 00:16:39.279
to get access to any of our data have to be
really transparent and upfront about when

00:16:39.279 --> 00:16:45.009
and how they are getting that data and importantly
exactly what they plan to do with it.

00:16:45.009 --> 00:16:48.629
They have to inform us in plain English too,
not legal soup.

00:16:48.629 --> 00:16:53.410
If you do still use Facebook then you may
have noticed this popup appearing recently

00:16:53.410 --> 00:16:59.350
upon logging in, that’s because the European
Court has forced them to do so under the GDPR.

00:16:59.350 --> 00:17:04.620
GDPR also gives European citizens the right
to write to any company that has collected

00:17:04.620 --> 00:17:07.630
their data and ask them to delete it permanently.

00:17:07.630 --> 00:17:14.850
Unbelievably, up until now, this hasn’t
actually been possible with most companies.

00:17:14.850 --> 00:17:20.399
You see, the way data storage solutions such
as SQL work means it’s so, so much easier

00:17:20.399 --> 00:17:26.600
for the company to just tick a box that hides
your data from the public instead of actually

00:17:26.600 --> 00:17:28.880
deleting it.

00:17:28.880 --> 00:17:34.120
So when you deactivate or delete your Facebook
account or any other online account, it and

00:17:34.120 --> 00:17:42.500
all the data surrounding it, still exists,
it’s just hidden, but such companies can

00:17:42.500 --> 00:17:45.669
still access it at any time.

00:17:45.669 --> 00:17:52.100
Unfortunately GDPR only effects European citizens
or any business based in Europe.

00:17:52.100 --> 00:17:57.350
But hold on, the saviest of tax avoiders out
there will know that to avoid billions of

00:17:57.350 --> 00:18:01.640
pounds of tax each year Facebook is technically
headquartered in Ireland.

00:18:01.640 --> 00:18:08.179
Yes, they exploit a legal tax loophole called
the “Double Irish Sandwich” to avoid paying

00:18:08.179 --> 00:18:13.130
corporation tax in all the countries they
operate in, which is basically all of the

00:18:13.130 --> 00:18:14.130
countries.

00:18:16.130 --> 00:18:20.660
So the totally American mega corporation Facebook
is on paper an Irish company.

